IRC Services -- a system of IRC services for IRC networks
---------------------------------------------------------

IRC Services is copyright (c) 1996-2009 Andrew Church.  There is absolutely
NO WARRANTY provided with this program; if it blows up in your face, you
get to clean up the mess.  Services is provided under the terms of the GNU
General Public License, version 2 or later, and may be freely redistributed,
with certain limitations described in that license (notably, if you
distribute IRC Services at all then you must distribute the source code as
well).  See the GNU General Public License (in the file GPL.txt) and the
relevant section of the manual (docs/readme.copyright).

---------------------------------------------------------------------------

This tree links to ircu2 (P10) networks; see BUILDING.md to build and
install it.  Documentation is located in the docs/ directory, one file per
topic:

    docs/readme.about      what Services are; list of the documents
    docs/readme.install    installing, running and controlling Services
    docs/readme.config     the configuration file: syntax and core settings
    docs/readme.modules    the settings of every module
    docs/readme.migration  converting an old ircservices.conf/modules.conf
    docs/readme.features   what Services do, feature by feature
    docs/readme.commands   every command of every pseudoclient
    docs/readme.database   PostgreSQL, Redis, and the database API for modules
    docs/readme.migrations the SQL that creates the tables; OperServ MIGRATION
    docs/readme.http       the HTTP server (Mongoose), and serving pages
    docs/readme.api        the configuration interface for module developers
    docs/readme.copyright  copyright and licenses
